title: Carriers
pid: 515abef1-fd9e-4494-95c6-98d2946d0119
body: |2-
  A side's tier is shown by one part of the side, its carrier: its
  numeral, if it shows one, and otherwise all its ancestor flags. The
  carrier shows the greater of its floor and the side's tier; every other
  glyph shows just its floor. On the forks in-side, whose tier is
  high, =2aK= shows the 2 high and the 'a' low, while =aK= has no
  numeral, so its 'a' carries the tier and is shown high.
